A||||1||Posthumane||Oil leak(s)||||1||
Z||000000||Posthumane||12-05-2001||02:59 AM||||When I was cleaning my engine the other day, I noticed that I had oil gathering around the PCV hose where it went into the head cover (84 2.5L). I always thought that it was probably just spillage left over from filling (hmmm... thought i cleaned that off....) but I when my engine got dusted over at a rallycross I noticed the oil seeping out of the elbow there. Question: Why would there be any oil going throught the PCV valve, let alone so much oil that it's actually leaking out? any thoughts?||||reg||1
Z||000001||deceler8||12-05-2001||09:07 AM||||On an old engine, the drainback holes on the head may be partially clogged which allows more oil to pool in the valve train area. The valve train can churn up this oil and send it into the PCV system. Also, an older engine can have more blowby as a result of normal wear. There may be more of the above than the PCV system can handle.<P>If you haven't, try resealing the valve cover and replacing the grommets in the valve cover for the PCV and breather. Also be sure the PCV valve is good and that the hoses aren't clogged/collapsed and/or leaking at the joints.||||reg||1
